id: pm-fokyhh
title: "Adopt Vitest 5 with CodSpeed 6.1, keeping exact coverage, benchmark history and the CodSpeed Axios patch"
description: "Own the Vitest 5.0.0 and @vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 major pair separately from routine dependency refreshes. The repository's mandatory @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 currently declares vitest ^3.2 || ^4, so adopting Vitest 5 would violate the installed performance-gate peer contract."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: codspeed,dependencies,peer-contract,testing
created_at: "2026-09-04T16:26:03.878Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T07:05:57.926Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T06:35:46.630Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T06:35:46.630Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A current @codspeed/vitest-plugin release accepts Vitest 5; Vitest and coverage-v8 are upgraded as an exact compatible pair; CodSpeed, full exact coverage, cross-platform CI, typecheck, static quality, packed consumers, and vulnerability gates pass."
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Upgraded vitest and @vitest/coverage-v8 to 5.0.5 with @codspeed/vitest-plugin 6.1.0 and Stryker 10.1.1. Ported the reviewed CodSpeed Axios removal to @codspeed/core 6.1.0 and refreshed its integrity policy; the runtime suite pins 30 exports. Migrated the three benchmark files to the bench fixture without changing CodSpeed URIs. Adapted the two SDK exemplar entry specs to the clearMocks default. coverage-v8 5 counts 93 more branches: two unreachable fallbacks were restructured so TypeScript narrows, and seven real gaps got tests."
expected_result: "Vitest 5 and coverage-v8 5 are adopted as a pair once CodSpeed accepts them, with every coverage, platform and packed-consumer gate green."
actual_result: "Full fast suite 11,757 passed; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with 55,557 of 55,557 branches; CodSpeed patch checker, runtime HTTP suite and walltime bench run pass; SDK mutation score 98.01 (345 killed, 7 equivalent); typecheck, ESLint, knip, docs/skills, tracker assurances and dependency advisories pass."
