comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T16:26:03.878Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status PM searches for Vitest 5, Vitest major, and CodSpeed peer compatibility found the closed compatible Vitest 4.1.11 refresh pm-n5ysuk and CodSpeed adoption pm-yh6t, but no owner for the 5.0.0 major. Live registry evidence on 2026-09-04: vitest 5.0.0 supports Node ^22.12 || ^24 || >=26, but mandatory @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 declares peer vitest ^3.2 || ^4. This item remains open and unclaimed until that external peer contract is compatible."
  "2026-09-05T03:52:26.679Z","harness:codex","Live 2026-09-05 registry verification: latest CodSpeed plugin still accepts Vitest ^3.2 || ^4, excluding available Vitest and coverage-v8 5.0.0. No compatible wanted update exists. Keep the canonical migration open and unclaimed; do not bypass the mandatory performance gate peer contract."
  "2026-09-06T05:33:02.832Z","harness:codex","2026-09-06 registry check: latest @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 still requires Vitest ^3.2 or ^4, excluding 5.0.0. Vitest and coverage-v8 major migration remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-09-08T08:10:07.397Z","harness:codex","2026-09-08 live registry check: latest @codspeed/vitest-plugin still declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4, excluding the Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 pair. No compatible wanted updates. Preserve the mandatory performance-gate peer contract; this canonical migration remains unclaimed."
  "2026-09-08T16:02:34.821Z","harness:codex","2026-09-08 afternoon registry verification: latest CodSpeed vitest-plugin 5.7.1 still declares vitest ^3.2 || ^4 and vite through ^7. Vitest 5 and coverage-v8 5 remain incompatible with the required performance harness. No compatible wanted upgrade; this canonical migration remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-09-08T16:13:02.051Z","harness:codex","Dependency eligibility verified against installed pnpm 11.10 source: default minimum-release-age is 24*60 minutes. typescript-eslint 8.70.0 published 2026-09-07T18:18Z remains inside that window at the afternoon verification; no exclusion or bypass added. TypeScript 7 remains outside the currently supported typescript-eslint range. Current pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities across 436 dependencies."
  "2026-09-10T05:01:06.278Z","harness:codex","2026-09-10 live registry verification: latest @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 requires vitest ^3.2 || ^4, excluding the available Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 pair. Preserve the mandatory performance harness peer contract; this canonical migration remains open and unclaimed. All compatible dependency updates are applied under pm-qs5iiq."
  "2026-09-10T18:23:47.301Z","harness:codex","Live 2026-09-10 evening registry check: @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 still declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4. The Vitest 5 and coverage-v8 5 pair remains outside the mandatory performance harness peer range. Retain this canonical unclaimed migration; no peer override added."
  "2026-09-11T06:30:50.428Z","harness:codex","2026-09-11 live dependency check: Vitest and coverage-v8 current/wanted remain 4.1.11; latest is 5.0.0. Registry-current @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 requires Vitest ^3.2 || ^4. Preserve the performance integration and this canonical unclaimed migration. Audit reports zero known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-11T10:21:12.176Z","harness:codex","Fresh registry verification 2026-09-11: @codspeed/vitest-plugin 5.7.1 still declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4. Full dependency audit returned zero vulnerabilities across 373 dependencies. Keep the existing major migration open and unclaimed; no peer override or duplicate item."
  "2026-09-12T07:25:58.759Z","harness:codex","2026-09-12 live registry check: latest CodSpeed plugin requires vitest ^3.2 || ^4. Preserve the mandatory performance integration; available Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 remains outside its peer range. pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-12T09:04:33.957Z","harness:codex","Fresh registry verification: CodSpeed vitest-plugin latest still supports Vitest ^3.2 or ^4, while registry Vitest and coverage-v8 latest are 5.0.0. pnpm reports current and wanted 4.1.11. Preserve the working performance-test integration and leave this migration open and unclaimed."
  "2026-09-13T09:20:58.462Z","harness:codex","2026-09-13 live compatibility check: Registry-current CodSpeed 5.7.1 still requires Vitest ^3.2 or ^4, excluding Vitest and coverage-v8 5.0.0. Preserve the existing open and unclaimed migration. Full dependency audit reports zero known vulnerabilities. Compatible patch and minor candidates are tracked separately in pm-7ej0mh."
  "2026-09-15T09:12:47.167Z","harness:codex","Registry verification 2026-09-15: latest CodSpeed plugin still requires Vitest ^3.2 or ^4 and excludes available Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0. No compatible wanted update. Keep this migration open and unclaimed; dependency audit is zero known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-18T03:05:30.630Z","harness:codex","2026-09-18 registry verification: latest CodSpeed plugin still requires Vitest ^3.2 or ^4, excluding Vitest and coverage-v8 5.0.1. Keep this canonical migration open and unclaimed; no peer override. Compatible wanted updates are empty and full pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-19T16:37:31.131Z","harness:codex","2026-09-19 registry check: CodSpeed latest still declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4, excluding Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.1. Retain the compatible pair and existing unclaimed migration. Full dependency audit reports zero known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-27T21:22:00.017Z","harness:codex","Live September 27 registry check: @codspeed/vitest-plugin latest 5.7.1 still declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4, excluding current latest Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.2. The canonical major migration remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-02T20:59:15.691Z","harness:codex","Live October 2 census: registry Vitest and coverage-v8 latest are 5.0.3, while installed CodSpeed plugin 5.7.1 still accepts only Vitest ^3.2 or ^4. Preserve the mandatory performance peer contract; this existing major migration stays open and unclaimed. Routine compatible MCP Apps 2.0.3 is now old enough for adoption and is tracked separately by pm-iktual."
  "2026-10-10T04:46:22.456Z","harness:codex","Fresh 2026-10-10 installed peer-contract inspection: CodSpeed vitest-plugin 5.7.1 declares vitest ^3.2 || ^4 and Vite through ^7, still excluding the available Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.3 pair. pnpm outdated reports current and wanted 4.1.11. Preserve this mandatory performance gate and existing canonical migration; no peer override or duplicate dependency item is added. Current source tests all pass, with one explicit-origin branch keeper being completed for exact coverage."
  "2026-10-12T23:01:17.203Z","harness:codex","Live installed peer recheck October12: CodSpeed vitest-plugin5.7.1 declares Vitest ^3.2 || ^4 and Vite through ^7. Latest Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.3 is old enough but still outside the required performance-plugin peer contract. Keep this existing migration open/unclaimed and retain the current4.1.11 pair."
  "2026-10-14T04:36:56.626Z","harness:codex","October14 dependency census: latest Vitest/coverage-v8 pair5.0.4 is1.8days old, below seven-day adoption. Installed CodSpeed vitest-plugin5.7.1 still excludes Vitest5 in its peer contract. Preserve4.1.11 and this canonical migration, without bypassing peers or performance gates."
  "2026-10-17T16:55:58.792Z","harness:codex","October17 live registry census: CodSpeed vitest-plugin6.1.0 now declares Vitest5 peers, removing the earlier upstream peer exclusion, but it is only one day old; Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.5 is two days old. Preserve4.1.11/5.7.1 until the seven-day cooldown and existing packed/runtime/performance acceptance gates can be met. No new duplicate or unreviewed major adoption."
  "2026-10-18T04:14:41.149Z","harness:codex","Fresh npm metadata at 2026-10-18 confirms @codspeed/vitest-plugin6.0.0 declares Vitest5 support, but publication is2026-10-13T15:46:05.308Z, and6.1.0 is2026-10-16T14:50:11.013Z. Both remain inside the unchanged seven-day cooldown; the previous peer-support gap is now a release-age boundary. Keep this canonical migration open and unclaimed until eligible, then verify actual instrument/native patch and runner compatibility before adoption."
  "2026-10-22T07:39:49.928Z","harness:codex","October22 refreshed registry evidence: latest Vitest and coverage-v8 5.0.5 were published October15 around14:28UTC, and CodSpeed6.1.0 on October16 at14:50UTC. Latest versions remain below seven full days at this intake. Keep the current patched4.1.12 pair and5.7.1 plugin while retaining this canonical migration open/unclaimed; adoption still requires actual runner/native-instrumentation and installed-consumer proof."
  "2026-10-24T12:19:08.879Z","harness:codex","October24 live registry update: Vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.5 (October15) and CodSpeed6.1.0 (October16) now exceed seven days. Latest CodSpeed declares Vitest5 peer support; Vitest5 engine range is ^22.12.0 || ^24.0.0 || >=26.0.0, so Node22.18 itself is admitted. Vite8.3.5 declares ^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0. Release age and these direct engine/peer declarations alone do not prove the repository runner, native instrumentation, coverage and installed-consumer acceptance. Preserve this canonical major migration open/unclaimed; the active SDK continuation delivery makes no toolchain migration claim."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T05:46:55.162Z","harness:claude-code","2026-11-01 adoption on branch chore/eligible-toolchain-and-bun-peers: vitest and @vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.5 (published 2026-10-15), @codspeed/vitest-plugin 6.1.0 (2026-10-16, peer vitest ^3.2 || ^4 || ^5), Stryker 10.1.1 (peer vitest >=2). @codspeed/core 6.1.0 still embeds Axios 1.4.0, so the pm-r61juc patch was ported: same replacement boundary (function bind$2 through the axios destructuring), 19,201 lines removed per entry, maps keep 5,293 mappings and drop 39,536, sources 131->21, maps newline-terminated; ESLint no-undef with inline config disabled finds no dangling identifier in either patched entry. Upstream 6.1.0 adds four Node-version warning exports, so the runtime suite now pins 30 exports. Transitive dev-only additions younger than seven days: magic-string 1.4.5 (via @vitest/mocker 5) and unbash 6.0.2 (via knip); both pass pnpm's supply-chain age policy."
  "2026-11-01T06:22:53.674Z","harness:claude-code","Vitest 5 removes the top-level bench() export (all three benchmark files failed with 'bench is not a function', which the CodSpeed workflow would have hit). Benchmarks now use the bench test fixture: each former describe group is a test of the same name that passes its registrations to bench.compare. CodSpeed 6.1.0's Vitest 5 provider keys results as <git-relative file>::<full test name>::<bench name>, and its legacy runner used <git-relative file>::<describe>::<bench>, so every benchmark URI and its history is unchanged. Verified locally: vitest bench --config vitest.bench.config.ts passes plain and with CODSPEED_ENV set in walltime mode."
  "2026-11-01T07:05:57.926Z","harness:claude-code","CodSpeed on PR 1646 reports -26% (6 regressed, 5 improved, neutral check) with no measured source changed. Cause: @codspeed/core 6.1.0 analysis mode adds --no-maglev (Node 24+) and --no-minor-gc-task to the existing --no-opt V8 flags, so hot loops (BM25 scoring, cursor encode/decode) are measured without the mid-tier compiler; CodSpeed itself tags all 11 as a different integration major, hardware and software environment. URIs are unchanged, so main's baseline resets to the 6.1 instrument on merge."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T05:46:56.471Z","harness:claude-code","Vitest 5 changes the clearMocks default to true: calls a spy records while the module under test is imported (vi.hoisted spy + top-level import) are cleared before the test body runs. Under Vitest 4 the full fast suite relied on this in exactly two specs (the SDK exemplar entry success/usage specs); record import-time effects into a plain array instead of reading mock.calls."
  "2026-11-01T06:05:34.322Z","harness:claude-code","@vitest/coverage-v8 5 counts 93 more branches than 4.1.12 on the same tree (55,560 vs 55,467 on main's merged coverage summary), mostly short-circuit operands of ||/&&/?? chains. Nine were unexercised: two were unreachable defensive fallbacks (the discovery cursor offset after Number.isInteger, and the background worker summary that evaluateWorkerResult always sets), restructured so TypeScript narrows instead of carrying a dead '??' branch; seven were real test gaps (field-state assurance filters for null, empty-string, empty-list and present values; replication sets and waivers without an owner; non-number and absent cursor offsets), now tested. Expect the next major coverage provider to surface similar residue: compare totals against the last main summary before writing tests."
